<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Autrigones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.) · capital Virovesca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A people of northern Burgos and western Bizkaia, whose towns Virovesca and Flaviobriga linked the Meseta to the Cantabrian Sea.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Autrigones occupied the land from the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> to the coast around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castro-urdiales">Castro Urdiales</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, Álava and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-biscay">Bizkaia</a>, from the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>. They bordered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cantabri">Cantabri</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turmodigi">Turmodigi</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caristii">Caristii</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/berones">Berones</a>, and their language was probably Celtic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in hillforts and lowland settlements, farming and herding, with towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/briviesca">Virovesca</a> (Briviesca) and Tritium Autrigonum named by Pliny and Ptolemy. Their political organisation is unknown.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> during the 1st century BCE, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> their territory became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hispania-tarraconensis">Hispania Tarraconensis</a>. The Flavian emperors founded the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castro-urdiales">Flaviobriga</a> on their coast, modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-castro">Castro</a> Urdiales.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 300 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:5.39%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Virovesca</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Autrigonians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-164&amp;focus=autrigones" aria-label="Autrigones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4599 665 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Autrigones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4919 921L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4919 921h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4919 921h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Virovesca. <a href="/atlas?year=-164&amp;focus=autrigones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
